# fm84 en français.
#
# Each msgid is the English as the code has it, and the msgstr under it what
# is shown in its place. A sentence with a count in it has a msgstr for each
# form the count takes: [one] for 0 and 1, [other] for the rest. A msgctxt
# sets one use of a word apart from the same word elsewhere. {name} is a
# place the program fills, kept as it is. The letters to press - Y, N, A and
# the like - stay as they are; the names of the keys are written as a French
# keyboard has them: Maj, Entrée, Échap, Suppr, Inser, Espace. A space comes
# before : and ?, and names are quoted « thus ».

